255 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 716 0 R
/E (In this Arduino program, a Hall sensor is connected to pin 2 \(HALL_PIN\), and two LEDs are connected to pins 6 \(LED_PIN1\) and 5 \(LED_PIN2\). The second LED works in the opposite way to the first LED.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [22]
>>
endobj
256 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 717 0 R
/E (The setup\(\) function runs once when the Arduino starts. It sets the Hall sensor pin as INPUT and both LED pins as OUTPUT using pinMode\(\).)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [23]
>>
endobj
257 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 718 0 R
/E (The loop\(\) function runs continuously. It reads the Hall sensor value using digitalRead\(\) and stores it in hallState.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [24]
>>
endobj
258 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 719 0 R
/E (If a magnet is detected \(LOW signal\), the LED on pin 6 turns ON and the LED on pin 5 turns OFF. If no magnet is present \(HIGH\), the LED on pin 6 turns OFF and the LED on pin 5 turns ON.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [25]
>>
endobj
259 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 85 0 R
/E (So overall, the Arduino detects a magnet using the Hall sensor and controls two LEDs in opposite ways.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [26]
>>
endobj
