361 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 746 0 R
/E (In this Arduino program, a Hall sensor is connected to pin 2 \(HALL_PIN\), a buzzer to pin 6 \(BUZZ_PIN\), and an LED to pin 5 \(LED_PIN\). The LED works in the opposite way to the buzzer.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [26]
>>
endobj
362 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 747 0 R
/E (The setup\(\) function runs once when the Arduino starts. It sets the Hall sensor as INPUT and both the buzzer and LED as OUTPUT using pinMode\(\). Initially, the buzzer is turned OFF and the LED is turned ON.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [27]
>>
endobj
363 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 748 0 R
/E (The loop\(\) function runs continuously. It reads the Hall sensor value using digitalRead\(\) and stores it in hallState.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [28]
>>
endobj
364 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 749 0 R
/E (If a magnet is detected \(LOW signal\), the buzzer turns ON and the LED turns OFF. If no magnet is present \(HIGH\), the buzzer turns OFF and the LED turns ON.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [29]
>>
endobj
365 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 750 0 R
/E (So overall, the Arduino detects a magnet and activates the buzzer while turning OFF the LED, and does the opposite when no magnet is present.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [30]
>>
endobj
