453 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 775 0 R
/E (In this Arduino program, a Hall sensor is connected to pin 2 \(HALL_PIN\), and two buzzers are connected to pins 6 and 5 \(BUZZ1_PIN and BUZZ2_PIN\).)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [24]
>>
endobj
454 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 776 0 R
/E (The setup\(\) function runs once when the Arduino starts. It sets the Hall sensor as INPUT and both buzzers as OUTPUT using pinMode\(\). Initially, both buzzers are turned OFF.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [25]
>>
endobj
455 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 777 0 R
/E (The loop\(\) function runs continuously. It reads the Hall sensor value using digitalRead\(\) and stores it in hallState.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [26]
>>
endobj
456 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 778 0 R
/E (If a magnet is detected \(LOW signal\), both buzzers turn ON. If no magnet is present \(HIGH\), both buzzers turn OFF.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [27]
>>
endobj
457 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 93 0 R
/E (So overall, the system activates both buzzers when a magnet is detected and turns them OFF otherwise.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [28]
>>
endobj
